/* Verse Games: THE WHOLE COUNSEL · 2 Kings chapters 1-5
   Verse text is filled/verified from the KJV by tools/fill-verses.js */
VG.registerBibleChapters("2kings", [
{n:1, name:"The Fall of Ahaziah", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 1:17",verse:"So he died according to the word of the LORD which Elijah had spoken. And Jehoram reigned in his stead in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah; because he had no son."}, facts:["Did you know Ahaziah fell through the lattice of his upper chamber in Samaria, and instead of seeking the God of Israel he sent messengers to Baal-zebub, the god of Ekron, a Philistine city (2 Kings 1:2)?","Did you know Elijah is described as 'an hairy man, and girt with a girdle of leather about his loins,' the same rugged dress later worn by John the Baptist (2 Kings 1:8)?","Did you know two captains and their hundred men were consumed by fire from heaven, but the third captain lived because he fell on his knees and pleaded for mercy (2 Kings 1:10-14)?"], questions:[
{q:"What happened between Moab and Israel after the death of Ahab?", options:["Moab rebelled against Israel","Moab paid double tribute","Moab made peace with Judah","Moab joined Israel against Syria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:1",verse:"Then Moab rebelled against Israel after the death of Ahab.", insight:"When a strong hand falls, old resentments rise; nations, like people, test every new boundary."},
{q:"How did Ahaziah's sickness begin?", options:["He fell through a lattice in his upper chamber in Samaria","He was wounded in battle with Moab","He caught a fever at the Jordan","He was poisoned at a feast"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:2",verse:"And Ahaziah fell down through a lattice in his upper chamber that was in Samaria, and was sick: and he sent messengers, and said unto them, Go, enquire of Baal-zebub the god of Ekron whether I shall recover of this disease.", insight:"A king's fall came through his own lattice; pride builds high chambers, and God lets them crack."},
{q:"To whom did Ahaziah send to learn whether he would recover?", options:["Baal-zebub the god of Ekron","The prophets of the LORD in Samaria","The priests of Bethel","The wise men of Damascus"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:2",verse:"And Ahaziah fell down through a lattice in his upper chamber that was in Samaria, and was sick: and he sent messengers, and said unto them, Go, enquire of Baal-zebub the god of Ekron whether I shall recover of this disease.", insight:"He passed over the God of Israel for a Philistine idol; the first question of faith is where you go for answers."},
{q:"Who told Elijah to go and meet the king's messengers?", options:["The angel of the LORD","The king of Judah","A prophet of Bethel","His servant Elisha"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:3",verse:"But the angel of the LORD said to Elijah the Tishbite, Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and say unto them, Is it not because there is not a God in Israel, that ye go to enquire of Baal-zebub the god of Ekron?", insight:"God intercepts the errand before it reaches the idol; heaven moves faster than messengers."},
{q:"What question did Elijah put to the king's messengers?", options:["Is it not because there is not a God in Israel?","Why does the king fear to die?","Who sent you from Samaria?","What gift will the king offer?"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:3",verse:"But the angel of the LORD said to Elijah the Tishbite, Arise, go up to meet the messengers of the king of Samaria, and say unto them, Is it not because there is not a God in Israel, that ye go to enquire of Baal-zebub the god of Ekron?", insight:"One question unmasks the whole errand; whenever you bypass God, this question still waits for you."},
{q:"What word did the LORD send to Ahaziah through Elijah?", options:["Thou shalt not come down from that bed, but shalt surely die","Thou shalt recover and reign forty years","Thou shalt be healed if thou repent","Thou shalt be carried to Ekron"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:4",verse:"Now therefore thus saith the LORD, Thou shalt not come down from that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die. And Elijah departed.", insight:"The bed he trusted became his sentence; God's word about sin is never a suggestion."},
{q:"What did Ahaziah ask when his messengers returned so soon?", options:["Why are ye now turned back?","What did Baal-zebub say?","Where is Elijah?","Did the priests bless me?"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:5",verse:"And when the messengers turned back unto him, he said unto them, Why are ye now turned back?", insight:"He expected an answer from Ekron and got one from heaven; God answers even the errands we send elsewhere."},
{q:"What did Ahaziah ask about the man who met his messengers?", options:["What manner of man was he?","What tribe was he from?","How old was he?","What did he wear on his head?"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:7",verse:"And he said unto them, What manner of man was he which came up to meet you, and told you these words?", insight:"The king wanted a description; God's messengers are known by their manner before their name."},
{q:"How did the messengers describe Elijah?", options:["An hairy man, girt with a girdle of leather about his loins","A tall man in a linen ephod","An old man with a golden staff","A young man in royal robes"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:8",verse:"And they answered him, He was an hairy man, and girt with a girdle of leather about his loins. And he said, It is Elijah the Tishbite.", insight:"Rough dress, unbending message; God does not costume His prophets to flatter courts."},
{q:"What did the first captain of fifty order Elijah to do?", options:["Come down, for the king hath said it","Come up to the palace at once","Flee from Samaria","Bless the king's army"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:9",verse:"Then the king sent unto him a captain of fifty with his fifty. And he went up to him: and, behold, he sat on the top of an hill. And he spake unto him, Thou man of God, the king hath said, Come down.", insight:"He spoke to God's prophet in a king's tone; borrowed authority sounds loud until heaven answers."},
{q:"How did Elijah answer the first captain?", options:["If I be a man of God, let fire come down from heaven and consume thee and thy fifty","I will come down after I pray","The king has no power over me","Let the king come up to me"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:10",verse:"And Elijah answered and said to the captain of fifty, If I be a man of God, then let fire come down from heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty. And there came down fire from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.", insight:"The test he named was God's to pass; never dare heaven unless heaven sent you."},
{q:"What order did the second captain add to the king's command?", options:["Come down quickly","Come down by night","Bring thy mantle with thee","Come down alone"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:11",verse:"Again also he sent unto him another captain of fifty with his fifty. And he answered and said unto him, O man of God, thus hath the king said, Come down quickly.", insight:"The second errand only hurried the first mistake; haste never fixes a wrong order."},
{q:"What befell the second captain and his fifty?", options:["The fire of God came down from heaven and consumed him and his fifty","They were struck blind on the hill","They fled and were scattered","They were taken captive by Elijah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:12",verse:"And Elijah answered and said unto them, If I be a man of God, let fire come down from heaven, and consume thee and thy fifty. And the fire of God came down from heaven, and consumed him and his fifty.", insight:"Judgment repeated is judgment confirmed; God does not change His answer because the question is louder."},
{q:"How did the third captain approach Elijah?", options:["He fell on his knees before Elijah and besought him","He surrounded the hill with archers","He sent a letter of warning","He waited seven days at the foot"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:13",verse:"And he sent again a captain of the third fifty with his fifty. And the third captain of fifty went up, and came and fell on his knees before Elijah, and besought him, and said unto him, O man of God, I pray thee, let my life, and the life of these fifty thy servants, be precious in thy sight.", insight:"Knees bend where commands failed; humility succeeds where force is burned up."},
{q:"What did the third captain plead for?", options:["That his life and the lives of his fifty be precious in Elijah's sight","That Elijah spare the king","That the fire fall on Ekron instead","That he be made a prophet"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:14",verse:"Behold, there came fire down from heaven, and burnt up the two captains of the former fifties with their fifties: therefore let my life now be precious in thy sight.", insight:"He had watched two fifties burn and learned the lesson; wise men learn from other men's ashes."},
{q:"What did the angel of the LORD say to Elijah about the third captain?", options:["Go down with him: be not afraid of him","Call fire upon him also","Send him back to the king","Hide thyself in the wilderness"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:15",verse:"And the angel of the LORD said unto Elijah, Go down with him: be not afraid of him. And he arose, and went down with him unto the king.", insight:"God distinguishes the humble from the proud, even in the same uniform; fear nothing when heaven bids you go."},
{q:"What did Elijah say to Ahaziah face to face?", options:["Because thou sent to Baal-zebub, thou shalt surely die","The LORD will heal thee in three days","Bring thy idols and I will pray","Thy son shall reign after thee"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:16",verse:"And he said unto him, Thus saith the LORD, Forasmuch as thou hast sent messengers to enquire of Baal-zebub the god of Ekron, is it not because there is no God in Israel to enquire of his word? therefore thou shalt not come down off that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die.", insight:"The prophet repeated heaven's sentence unchanged; God's word does not soften between the hill and the palace."},
{q:"How was the word of the LORD fulfilled upon Ahaziah?", options:["He died according to the word which Elijah had spoken","He recovered and repented","He fled to Ekron and died there","He was slain by his servants"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:17",verse:"So he died according to the word of the LORD which Elijah had spoken. And Jehoram reigned in his stead in the second year of Jehoram the son of Jehoshaphat king of Judah; because he had no son.", insight:"Scripture ties the death to the word; when God speaks, the ending is already written."},
{q:"What did Elijah do after delivering the LORD's word to the messengers?", options:["And Elijah departed","He went with them to Samaria","He waited for the king's reply","He prayed for Ahaziah's healing"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:4",verse:"Now therefore thus saith the LORD, Thou shalt not come down from that bed on which thou art gone up, but shalt surely die. And Elijah departed.", insight:"He delivered the word and departed; the prophet's task is to speak, not to stay and watch."},
{q:"Where are the rest of Ahaziah's acts recorded?", options:["In the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel","In the book of Jasher","In the records of Ekron","In the annals of the prophets"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 1:18",verse:"Now the rest of the acts of Ahaziah which he did, are they not written in the book of the chronicles of the kings of Israel?", insight:"Kings keep chronicles, but heaven keeps the truer record; live for the book that lasts."}
]},
{n:2, name:"Elijah Taken Up", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 2:11",verse:"And it came to pass, as they still went on, and talked, that, behold, there appeared a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and parted them both asunder; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven."}, facts:["Did you know Elisha refused three times to leave Elijah, swearing, 'As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee,' at Gilgal, Bethel, and Jericho (2 Kings 2:2-6)?","Did you know Elisha healed Jericho's bad water with salt in a new cruse, and the waters were healed 'unto this day' (2 Kings 2:20-22)?","Did you know the two she bears tore forty and two of the young men who mocked Elisha with the cry, 'Go up, thou bald head' (2 Kings 2:23-24)?"], questions:[
{q:"How was the LORD about to take Elijah into heaven?", options:["By a whirlwind","In a cloud of glory","On a mountain of fire","Through the Red Sea"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:1",verse:"And it came to pass, when the LORD would take up Elijah into heaven by a whirlwind, that Elijah went with Elisha from Gilgal.", insight:"No grave for Elijah, only a whirlwind; God writes some endings without death."},
{q:"What did Elisha answer when Elijah told him to tarry at Gilgal?", options:["As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee","Go in peace, my master","I will wait until thou return","Send for me at Bethel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:2",verse:"And Elijah said unto Elisha, Tarry here, I pray thee; for the LORD hath sent me to Bethel. And Elisha said unto him, As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. So they went down to Bethel.", insight:"Three times tested, three times faithful; devotion that will not be dismissed inherits the blessing."},
{q:"What did the sons of the prophets at Bethel tell Elisha?", options:["The LORD will take away thy master from thy head to day","Elijah will anoint thee king","The Jordan will overflow tonight","Fifty men will follow thee"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:3",verse:"And the sons of the prophets that were at Bethel came forth to Elisha, and said unto him, Knowest thou that the LORD will take away thy master from thy head to day? And he said, Yea, I know it; hold ye your peace.", insight:"Others can see your loss coming; Elisha knew it too, and still would not leave."},
{q:"To what place did Elijah journey last of all?", options:["To Jordan","To Carmel","To Samaria","To Damascus"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:6",verse:"And Elijah said unto him, Tarry, I pray thee, here; for the LORD hath sent me to Jordan. And he said, As the LORD liveth, and as thy soul liveth, I will not leave thee. And they two went on.", insight:"The last stop was the river; God often finishes at the waters He once parted."},
{q:"How many of the sons of the prophets watched from afar at the Jordan?", options:["Fifty men","Twelve men","Seven men","A hundred men"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:7",verse:"And fifty men of the sons of the prophets went, and stood to view afar off: and they two stood by Jordan.", insight:"Fifty watched from afar, one walked beside; closeness to God's work is a choice, not a crowd."},
{q:"How did Elijah part the waters of the Jordan?", options:["He wrapped his mantle together and smote the waters","He stretched out his rod","He prayed and the wind dried it","He cast salt into the stream"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:8",verse:"And Elijah took his mantle, and wrapped it together, and smote the waters, and they were divided hither and thither, so that they two went over on dry ground.", insight:"The mantle was only cloth until faith wrapped it; God works through surrendered things."},
{q:"What did Elijah invite Elisha to ask before he was taken?", options:["Ask what I shall do for thee, before I be taken away from thee","Ask for gold and silver","Ask to return to Gilgal","Ask for a quiet life"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:9",verse:"And it came to pass, when they were gone over, that Elijah said unto Elisha, Ask what I shall do for thee, before I be taken away from thee. And Elisha said, I pray thee, let a double portion of thy spirit be upon me.", insight:"A parting master opens his hands; ask for the eternal when the moment is holy."},
{q:"What did Elisha request of Elijah?", options:["A double portion of thy spirit be upon me","To see heaven opened","To escape death like thee","To rule over Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:9",verse:"And it came to pass, when they were gone over, that Elijah said unto Elisha, Ask what I shall do for thee, before I be taken away from thee. And Elisha said, I pray thee, let a double portion of thy spirit be upon me.", insight:"He did not ask for Elijah's miracles but his spirit; ask for the Source, not the signs."},
{q:"On what condition would Elisha receive the double portion?", options:["If thou see me when I am taken from thee","If thou fast forty days","If thou cross Jordan alone","If thou anoint three kings"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:10",verse:"And he said, Thou hast asked a hard thing: nevertheless, if thou see me when I am taken from thee, it shall be so unto thee; but if not, it shall not be so.", insight:"The blessing hinged on watching; keep your eyes on heaven and you will not miss the gift."},
{q:"What appeared and parted Elijah and Elisha as they walked and talked?", options:["A chariot of fire, and horses of fire","A pillar of cloud","A host of angels with swords","A great earthquake"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:11",verse:"And it came to pass, as they still went on, and talked, that, behold, there appeared a chariot of fire, and horses of fire, and parted them both asunder; and Elijah went up by a whirlwind into heaven.", insight:"Fire that parts is still mercy; heaven's escort came between them so glory could carry one away."},
{q:"What did Elisha cry as Elijah went up?", options:["My father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof","Stay with me, my master","Blessed be the name of the LORD","Take me with thee"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:12",verse:"And Elisha saw it, and he cried, My father, my father, the chariot of Israel, and the horsemen thereof. And he saw him no more: and he took hold of his own clothes, and rent them in two pieces.", insight:"He named Elijah Israel's true defense; one man of God outweighs chariots and horsemen."},
{q:"What fell from Elijah that Elisha took up?", options:["His mantle","His girdle","His staff","His sandals"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:13",verse:"He took up also the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and went back, and stood by the bank of Jordan;", insight:"The mantle fell, the ministry continued; God's work outlives God's workers."},
{q:"What did Elisha cry as he smote the Jordan with the mantle?", options:["Where is the LORD God of Elijah?","Part, ye waters, for Elisha","Remember thy servant Moses","Let the river praise the LORD"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:14",verse:"And he took the mantle of Elijah that fell from him, and smote the waters, and said, Where is the LORD God of Elijah? and when he also had smitten the waters, they parted hither and thither: and Elisha went over.", insight:"His first act was to call on Elijah's God, not his own power; the right question opens every river."},
{q:"What did the sons of the prophets say when they saw Elisha part the water?", options:["The spirit of Elijah doth rest on Elisha","Elisha is greater than Elijah","The LORD has forsaken us","Let us follow the whirlwind"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:15",verse:"And when the sons of the prophets which were to view at Jericho saw him, they said, The spirit of Elijah doth rest on Elisha. And they came to meet him, and bowed themselves to the ground before him.", insight:"The sign confirmed the succession; God lets witnesses see when He passes the torch."},
{q:"What did the prophets fear had become of Elijah's body?", options:["The Spirit of the LORD had cast him upon some mountain, or into some valley","The whirlwind had carried him to heaven bodily","Wild beasts had devoured him","He had hidden in a cave"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:16",verse:"And they said unto him, Behold now, there be with thy servants fifty strong men; let them go, we pray thee, and seek thy master: lest peradventure the Spirit of the LORD hath taken him up, and cast him upon some mountain, or into some valley. And he said, Ye shall not send.", insight:"They sought a body where God had given glory; faith sometimes looks for what heaven has lifted."},
{q:"How long did the fifty men search for Elijah?", options:["Three days, but found him not","Seven days","Forty days","One day"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:17",verse:"And when they urged him till he was ashamed, he said, Send. They sent therefore fifty men; and they sought three days, but found him not.", insight:"Three days of searching proved what Elisha already knew; obedience is wiser than investigation."},
{q:"What was wrong with the water at Jericho?", options:["The water was naught, and the ground barren","The wells had run dry","The river was poisoned","The springs were bitter with salt"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:19",verse:"And the men of the city said unto Elisha, Behold, I pray thee, the situation of this city is pleasant, as my lord seeth: but the water is naught, and the ground barren.", insight:"A pleasant city with deadly water; fair settings can hide deep corruption."},
{q:"What did Elisha ask for to heal the water?", options:["A new cruse, with salt therein","An old wineskin of oil","Seven stones from the river","A branch of hyssop"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:20",verse:"And he said, Bring me a new cruse, and put salt therein. And they bring it to him.", insight:"Salt in a new vessel for bitter waters; God heals with the humblest means."},
{q:"What did the mockers cry at Elisha on the way to Bethel?", options:["Go up, thou bald head; go up, thou bald head","Go back to the Jordan","Where is thy master now?","Show us a sign, prophet"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:23",verse:"And he went up from thence unto Bethel: and as he was going up by the way, there came forth little children out of the city, and mocked him, and said unto him, Go up, thou bald head; go up, thou bald head.", insight:"They mocked the prophet's going up, who had just seen Elijah go up; contempt for God's servants is contempt for God."},
{q:"What came out of the wood against the mockers?", options:["Two she bears, which tare forty and two of them","A lion from the thicket","A swarm of hornets","A band of robbers"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 2:24",verse:"And he turned back, and looked on them, and cursed them in the name of the LORD. And there came forth two she bears out of the wood, and tare forty and two children of them.", insight:"The curse in the LORD's name was answered from the wood; dishonouring God's messenger carries a fearful price."}
]},
{n:3, name:"War Against Moab", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 3:18",verse:"And this is but a light thing in the sight of the LORD: he will deliver the Moabites also into your hand."}, facts:["Did you know Mesha, king of Moab, paid Israel a yearly tribute of a hundred thousand lambs and a hundred thousand rams with the wool, and his rebellion is recorded on the famous Mesha Stele (2 Kings 3:4)?","Did you know the water came at the very hour of the morning sacrifice, 'when the meat offering was offered,' with no wind and no rain (2 Kings 3:17, 20)?","Did you know the Moabites mistook the sunrise on the water for blood and shouted, 'Moab, to the spoil,' rushing to a defeat they had imagined as a victory (2 Kings 3:22-23)?"], questions:[
{q:"Who became king of Israel after the death of Ahaziah?", options:["Jehoram the son of Ahab","Ahaziah's son","Jehu","Athaliah"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:1",verse:"Now Jehoram the son of Ahab began to reign over Israel in Samaria the eighteenth year of Jehoshaphat king of Judah, and reigned twelve years.", insight:"A new king, an old rebellion; thrones change, but only God changes hearts."},
{q:"In what way was Jehoram better than Ahab and Jezebel?", options:["He put away the image of Baal that his father had made","He destroyed all the high places","He restored true worship in Israel","He tore down the calves at Bethel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:2",verse:"And he wrought evil in the sight of the LORD; but not like his father, and like his mother: for he put away the image of Baal that his father had made.", insight:"Half reform is still half; removing one idol while keeping another is not repentance."},
{q:"To what sin did Jehoram cling?", options:["The sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, which made Israel to sin","The worship of Baal","The gods of the Syrians","The idols of Ekron"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:3",verse:"Nevertheless he cleaved unto the sins of Jeroboam the son of Nebat, which made Israel to sin; he departed not therefrom.", insight:"He quit Baal but kept Jeroboam's calves; partial obedience is polished disobedience."},
{q:"What tribute had Mesha king of Moab paid to Israel?", options:["An hundred thousand lambs, and an hundred thousand rams, with the wool","Ten talents of gold","A thousand horses","Fifty thousand measures of wheat"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:4",verse:"And Mesha king of Moab was a sheepmaster, and rendered unto the king of Israel an hundred thousand lambs, and an hundred thousand rams, with the wool.", insight:"Moab's wealth was counted in sheep; God measures tribute, but He weighs the heart."},
{q:"What answer did Jehoshaphat give to Jehoram's call to war?", options:["I will go up: I am as thou art, my people as thy people","I will send my servants only","Let Israel fight alone","Wait until the spring rains"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:7",verse:"And he went and sent to Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, saying, The king of Moab hath rebelled against me: wilt thou go with me against Moab to battle? And he said, I will go up: I am as thou art, my people as thy people, and my horses as thy horses.", insight:"Jehoshaphat allied too quickly again; good kings still need godly counsel before marching."},
{q:"By which way did the allied kings march against Moab?", options:["The way through the wilderness of Edom","The king's highway through Moab","Along the Jordan valley","By ships from Joppa"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:8",verse:"And he said, Which way shall we go up? And he answered, The way through the wilderness of Edom.", insight:"They chose the desert road and found its thirst; shortcuts through the wilderness are never short."},
{q:"What crisis struck the three armies after seven days' march?", options:["There was no water for the host, nor for the cattle","Their food ran out","The Edomites deserted","A plague broke out"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:9",verse:"So the king of Israel went, and the king of Judah, and the king of Edom: and they fetched a compass of seven days’ journey: and there was no water for the host, and for the cattle that followed them.", insight:"Seven days of marching, then empty skins; God lets armies thirst so kings will seek Him."},
{q:"What did the king of Israel cry when the water failed?", options:["Alas! that the LORD hath called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Moab!","The LORD has forsaken us","Let us return to Samaria","Moab's gods are stronger"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:10",verse:"And the king of Israel said, Alas! that the LORD hath called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Moab!", insight:"He blamed God for the trouble his own march had made; despair accuses before it enquires."},
{q:"How was Elisha described to the kings?", options:["He which poured water on the hands of Elijah","The prophet of Bethel","The son of the priest","The seer of Samaria"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:11",verse:"But Jehoshaphat said, Is there not here a prophet of the LORD, that we may enquire of the LORD by him? And one of the king of Israel’s servants answered and said, Here is Elisha the son of Shaphat, which poured water on the hands of Elijah.", insight:"Known as Elijah's servant first; greatness in God's kingdom begins with pouring water."},
{q:"What did Elisha say to the king of Israel?", options:["What have I to do with thee? get thee to the prophets of thy father","I will not speak to idolaters","Pay me and I will prophesy","Return to Samaria at once"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:13",verse:"And Elisha said unto the king of Israel, What have I to do with thee? get thee to the prophets of thy father, and to the prophets of thy mother. And the king of Israel said unto him, Nay: for the LORD hath called these three kings together, to deliver them into the hand of Moab.", insight:"The prophet refused a polite hearing; you cannot consult God while courting idols."},
{q:"Why did Elisha consent to speak at all?", options:["He regarded the presence of Jehoshaphat the king of Judah","The king of Israel repented","The soldiers begged him","He feared the Moabites"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:14",verse:"And Elisha said, As the LORD of hosts liveth, before whom I stand, surely, were it not that I regard the presence of Jehoshaphat the king of Judah, I would not look toward thee, nor see thee.", insight:"One godly man in the camp opened heaven for all; righteousness in the company is never wasted."},
{q:"What did Elisha call for before he prophesied?", options:["A minstrel","A sacrifice","Silence","His mantle"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:15",verse:"But now bring me a minstrel. And it came to pass, when the minstrel played, that the hand of the LORD came upon him.", insight:"Music prepared the prophet's heart; worship tunes the soul to hear God."},
{q:"What was Elisha's strange command?", options:["Make this valley full of ditches","Dig a well in the camp","March back to the Jordan","Fill your vessels with sand"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:16",verse:"And he said, Thus saith the LORD, Make this valley full of ditches.", insight:"Dig ditches before you see water; faith prepares for the blessing it cannot yet see."},
{q:"How would the water come, according to the word of the LORD?", options:["Ye shall not see wind, neither shall ye see rain; yet that valley shall be filled with water","A great rain would fall at midnight","A spring would burst in the camp","The Jordan would turn aside"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:17",verse:"For thus saith the LORD, Ye shall not see wind, neither shall ye see rain; yet that valley shall be filled with water, that ye may drink, both ye, and your cattle, and your beasts.", insight:"No wind, no rain, yet full; God is not bound to the means He usually uses."},
{q:"What did Elisha say was but a light thing to the LORD?", options:["Filling the valley with water; He would also deliver the Moabites into their hand","Feeding the whole army","Healing the sick","Sending rain on Edom"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:18",verse:"And this is but a light thing in the sight of the LORD: he will deliver the Moabites also into your hand.", insight:"Water was the small gift; victory was the greater. God's 'light things' are our impossibilities."},
{q:"When did the water arrive?", options:["In the morning, when the meat offering was offered","At midnight","At the third watch","When the sun stood still"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:20",verse:"And it came to pass in the morning, when the meat offering was offered, that, behold, there came water by the way of Edom, and the country was filled with water.", insight:"At the hour of worship the water came; heaven keeps time with the altar."},
{q:"What did the Moabites see when the sun shone on the water?", options:["The water as red as blood","An army of angels","Their own faces","The kings fleeing"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:22",verse:"And they rose up early in the morning, and the sun shone upon the water, and the Moabites saw the water on the other side as red as blood:", insight:"Sunrise turned water to seeming blood; God can make nature itself deceive His enemies."},
{q:"What did the Moabites conclude, and what did they shout?", options:["The kings have slain one another: now therefore, Moab, to the spoil","The gods have turned the river to blood: flee","Israel is retreating: pursue them","The Edomites have betrayed us"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:23",verse:"And they said, This is blood: the kings are surely slain, and they have smitten one another: now therefore, Moab, to the spoil.", insight:"They ran to plunder and found a battle; presumption reads every sign in its own favor."},
{q:"How many swordsmen did the king of Moab take to break through to the king of Edom?", options:["Seven hundred men that drew swords","Three hundred","A thousand","Fifty"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:26",verse:"And when the king of Moab saw that the battle was too sore for him, he took with him seven hundred men that drew swords, to break through even unto the king of Edom: but they could not.", insight:"Seven hundred swords could not cut a way out; when God shuts the battle, no courage reopens it."},
{q:"What dreadful act did the king of Moab commit on the wall?", options:["He offered his eldest son for a burnt offering","He cast his crown to Israel","He slew his own captains","He burned the city gates"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 3:27",verse:"Then he took his eldest son that should have reigned in his stead, and offered him for a burnt offering upon the wall. And there was great indignation against Israel: and they departed from him, and returned to their own land.", insight:"Desperation sacrificed his own heir; idolatry always demands what is dearest in the end."}
]},
{n:4, name:"The Shunammite's Son", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 4:35",verse:"Then he returned, and walked in the house to and fro; and went up, and stretched himself upon him: and the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes."}, facts:["Did you know the widow's oil kept flowing until every borrowed vessel was full, and stopped the moment there was 'not a vessel more' (2 Kings 4:6)?","Did you know the Shunammite's son sneezed seven times and opened his eyes after Elisha stretched himself upon the child and prayed (2 Kings 4:34-35)?","Did you know twenty loaves of barley fed a hundred men with food left over, 'according to the word of the LORD' (2 Kings 4:43-44)?"], questions:[
{q:"What danger threatened the widow's two sons?", options:["The creditor was come to take them to be bondmen","The king would make them soldiers","Famine would starve them","The Syrians would carry them away"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:1",verse:"Now there cried a certain woman of the wives of the sons of the prophets unto Elisha, saying, Thy servant my husband is dead; and thou knowest that thy servant did fear the LORD: and the creditor is come to take unto him my two sons to be bondmen.", insight:"Debt reached for her children; God hears the widow before the creditor knocks."},
{q:"What did the widow have left in her house?", options:["Nothing, save a pot of oil","A handful of meal","Two small fishes","An empty purse"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:2",verse:"And Elisha said unto her, What shall I do for thee? tell me, what hast thou in the house? And she said, Thine handmaid hath not any thing in the house, save a pot of oil.", insight:"A pot of oil was all; God loves to start with 'almost nothing.'"},
{q:"What did Elisha tell her to borrow from her neighbours?", options:["Empty vessels; borrow not a few","Silver and gold","Bread for her sons","Oil to fill them"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:3",verse:"Then he said, Go, borrow thee vessels abroad of all thy neighbours, even empty vessels; borrow not a few.", insight:"'Borrow not a few'; the measure of the miracle was the measure of her gathering."},
{q:"When did the oil stop flowing?", options:["When there was not a vessel more","At sunset","When her sons grew tired","When Elisha returned"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:6",verse:"And it came to pass, when the vessels were full, that she said unto her son, Bring me yet a vessel. And he said unto her, There is not a vessel more. And the oil stayed.", insight:"The oil stopped only when the vessels ran out; God's supply outlasts our capacity, never His willingness."},
{q:"What did Elisha tell her to do with the oil?", options:["Go, sell the oil, and pay thy debt, and live of the rest","Pour it out as an offering","Give it to the prophets","Keep it for the famine"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:7",verse:"Then she came and told the man of God. And he said, Go, sell the oil, and pay thy debt, and live thou and thy children of the rest.", insight:"Pay the debt first, then live; God's provision restores duty before comfort."},
{q:"In what town did the great woman live who fed Elisha?", options:["Shunem","Bethel","Gilgal","Jericho"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:8",verse:"And it fell on a day, that Elisha passed to Shunem, where was a great woman; and she constrained him to eat bread. And so it was, that as oft as he passed by, he turned in thither to eat bread.", insight:"A great woman in a small town; God finds generous hearts in quiet places."},
{q:"What did the woman perceive about Elisha?", options:["That he was an holy man of God","That he was a king in disguise","That he was Elijah returned","That he was a rich merchant"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:9",verse:"And she said unto her husband, Behold now, I perceive that this is an holy man of God, which passeth by us continually.", insight:"She discerned holiness by watching his life; character is the prophet's true credential."},
{q:"What four things did she set in the little chamber on the wall?", options:["A bed, and a table, and a stool, and a candlestick","A bed, a chest, a lamp, and a rug","A table, two chairs, a lamp, and bread","A couch, a desk, a candle, and wine"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:10",verse:"Let us make a little chamber, I pray thee, on the wall; and let us set for him there a bed, and a table, and a stool, and a candlestick: and it shall be, when he cometh to us, that he shall turn in thither.", insight:"Bed, table, stool, candlestick; simple hospitality made room for the holy."},
{q:"What did the Shunammite answer when offered the king's favor?", options:["I dwell among mine own people","Make me a prophetess","Give me gold instead","Let my son serve the king"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:13",verse:"And he said unto him, Say now unto her, Behold, thou hast been careful for us with all this care; what is to be done for thee? wouldest thou be spoken for to the king, or to the captain of the host? And she answered, I dwell among mine own people.", insight:"Content among her own people, she wanted no court favor; enough is a quiet kind of wealth."},
{q:"What did Gehazi say the woman lacked?", options:["She hath no child, and her husband is old","She hath no husband","She hath no house of her own","She hath no servant"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:14",verse:"And he said, What then is to be done for her? And Gehazi answered, Verily she hath no child, and her husband is old.", insight:"The servant saw the hidden sorrow; God often answers the grief we never voice."},
{q:"What promise did Elisha make to the Shunammite?", options:["About this season, thou shalt embrace a son","Thy husband shall be healed","Thy house shall be spared in famine","Thou shalt see thy grandchildren"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:16",verse:"And he said, About this season, according to the time of life, thou shalt embrace a son. And she said, Nay, my lord, thou man of God, do not lie unto thine handmaid.", insight:"A son to the childless, at the set season; God's promises keep heaven's calendar, not ours."},
{q:"What happened to the boy out in the harvest field?", options:["He cried, My head, my head, and died at noon on his mother's knees","He was bitten by a serpent","He fell from a wagon","He was struck by lightning"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:19",verse:"And he said unto his father, My head, my head. And he said to a lad, Carry him to his mother.", insight:"Joy turned to grief in a morning; the gifts of God are held, not owned."},
{q:"Where did the grieving mother lay her dead son?", options:["On the bed of the man of God","In her own chamber","In the field","In a tomb"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:21",verse:"And she went up, and laid him on the bed of the man of God, and shut the door upon him, and went out.", insight:"She laid him where the holy man had slept; grief that runs to God is already on the way to hope."},
{q:"What did the Shunammite answer when asked if all was well?", options:["It is well","My son is dead","I am ruined","Pray for me"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:26",verse:"Run now, I pray thee, to meet her, and say unto her, Is it well with thee? is it well with thy husband? is it well with the child? And she answered, It is well.", insight:"'It is well' from a breaking heart; faith can speak peace before it feels it."},
{q:"What charge did Elisha give Gehazi as he sent him ahead?", options:["Gird up thy loins, take my staff, salute no man by the way, and lay the staff on the child's face","Run and fetch the physicians","Tell no one what has happened","Bring the child's father"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:29",verse:"Then he said to Gehazi, Gird up thy loins, and take my staff in thine hand, and go thy way: if thou meet any man, salute him not; and if any salute thee, answer him not again: and lay my staff upon the face of the child.", insight:"No greetings by the way; urgent mercy does not stop for courtesy."},
{q:"What happened when Gehazi laid the staff on the child's face?", options:["There was neither voice, nor hearing","The child opened his eyes","The staff broke in two","A wind filled the room"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:31",verse:"And Gehazi passed on before them, and laid the staff upon the face of the child; but there was neither voice, nor hearing. Wherefore he went again to meet him, and told him, saying, The child is not awaked.", insight:"The staff without the prophet was only wood; instruments cannot replace intercession."},
{q:"What did Elisha do alone in the chamber with the dead child?", options:["He shut the door upon them twain, and prayed unto the LORD","He anointed him with oil","He called the neighbours to mourn","He sent for the priests"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:33",verse:"He went in therefore, and shut the door upon them twain, and prayed unto the LORD.", insight:"Shut door, open heaven; some miracles are born only in secret prayer."},
{q:"What showed that the boy lived again?", options:["He sneezed seven times, and opened his eyes","He sat up and spoke","He walked to his mother","He laughed aloud"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:35",verse:"Then he returned, and walked in the house to and fro; and went up, and stretched himself upon him: and the child sneezed seven times, and the child opened his eyes.", insight:"Seven sneezes, then open eyes; life returns in God's own rhythm, not ours."},
{q:"What did the prophets cry when they tasted the pottage?", options:["O thou man of God, there is death in the pot","This pottage is bitter","The pot is empty","Bless this food"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:40",verse:"So they poured out for the men to eat. And it came to pass, as they were eating of the pottage, that they cried out, and said, O thou man of God, there is death in the pot. And they could not eat thereof.", insight:"They tasted death and cried out; honesty about the poison is the first step to the cure."},
{q:"What came of the twenty loaves of barley?", options:["They did eat, and left thereof, according to the word of the LORD","They were not enough for the men","They were stored for the famine","They were given to the poor only"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 4:44",verse:"So he set it before them, and they did eat, and left thereof, according to the word of the LORD.", insight:"Twenty loaves fed a hundred with leftovers; God's arithmetic multiplies what is given."}
]},
{n:5, name:"Naaman's Healing", seal:{ref:"2 Kings 5:15",verse:"And he returned to the man of God, he and all his company, and came, and stood before him: and he said, Behold, now I know that there is no God in all earth, but in Israel: now therefore, I pray thee, take a blessing of thy servant."}, facts:["Did you know the good news of this chapter begins with a little captive maid, whose simple words, 'Would God my lord were with the prophet,' set Naaman on the road to healing (2 Kings 5:2-3)?","Did you know Naaman asked for two mules' burden of Israel's earth so he could worship the LORD on holy ground back in Syria (2 Kings 5:17)?","Did you know Gehazi's greed cost him Naaman's leprosy, which would cleave to him and his seed for ever, and he went out 'a leper as white as snow' (2 Kings 5:27)?"], questions:[
{q:"What is said of Naaman besides his greatness and honour?", options:["He was a mighty man in valour, but he was a leper","He was a prophet of Syria","He was the king's son","He was a friend of Elisha"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:1",verse:"Now Naaman, captain of the host of the king of Syria, was a great man with his master, and honourable, because by him the LORD had given deliverance unto Syria: he was also a mighty man in valour, but he was a leper.", insight:"Mighty in valour, marred by leprosy; every strength has its hidden wound, and only God heals the hidden ones."},
{q:"Who first spoke of the prophet to Naaman's household?", options:["A little maid, captive out of the land of Israel","Naaman's wife","The king of Syria","A Syrian captain"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:2",verse:"And the Syrians had gone out by companies, and had brought away captive out of the land of Israel a little maid; and she waited on Naaman’s wife.", insight:"A captive child carried the gospel to a captain; God uses the smallest voices for the greatest errands."},
{q:"What did the little maid say?", options:["Would God my lord were with the prophet that is in Samaria! for he would recover him of his leprosy","Let my lord go to Damascus","The gods of Syria can heal","Send for the physicians"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:3",verse:"And she said unto her mistress, Would God my lord were with the prophet that is in Samaria! for he would recover him of his leprosy.", insight:"One sentence of faith from a servant girl; never despise the witness of the lowly."},
{q:"What did Naaman take with him to Israel?", options:["Ten talents of silver, and six thousand pieces of gold, and ten changes of raiment","A hundred talents of silver","Horses and chariots","Spices and jewels"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:5",verse:"And the king of Syria said, Go to, go, and I will send a letter unto the king of Israel. And he departed, and took with him ten talents of silver, and six thousand pieces of gold, and ten changes of raiment.", insight:"He packed wealth for a healing; grace cannot be bought, only received."},
{q:"What did the king of Syria's letter require of the king of Israel?", options:["That thou mayest recover Naaman my servant of his leprosy","That thou send thy army to Damascus","That thou pay tribute to Syria","That thou release the captives"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:6",verse:"And he brought the letter to the king of Israel, saying, Now when this letter is come unto thee, behold, I have therewith sent Naaman my servant to thee, that thou mayest recover him of his leprosy.", insight:"A king commanded a miracle by letter; men mistake authority for ability."},
{q:"What did the king of Israel cry when he read the letter?", options:["Am I God, to kill and to make alive?","I will do as Syria asks","Call the prophets together","This is a trick of war"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:7",verse:"And it came to pass, when the king of Israel had read the letter, that he rent his clothes, and said, Am I God, to kill and to make alive, that this man doth send unto me to recover a man of his leprosy? wherefore consider, I pray you, and see how he seeketh a quarrel against me.", insight:"He tore his clothes in despair; the right question asked in panic still points to the true God."},
{q:"What message did Elisha send to the king?", options:["Let him come now to me, and he shall know that there is a prophet in Israel","Send Naaman back to Syria","I cannot help him","Bring him to the palace"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:8",verse:"And it was so, when Elisha the man of God had heard that the king of Israel had rent his clothes, that he sent to the king, saying, Wherefore hast thou rent thy clothes? let him come now to me, and he shall know that there is a prophet in Israel.", insight:"The prophet steadied a panicking king; God's servants calm what kings cannot."},
{q:"How did Elisha deliver his instruction to Naaman?", options:["He sent a messenger unto him","He came out himself","He wrote him a letter","He met him at the Jordan"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:10",verse:"And Elisha sent a messenger unto him, saying, Go and wash in the Jordan seven times, and thy flesh shall come again to thee, and thou shalt be clean.", insight:"No ceremony, only a messenger; God often heals without the theatre we expect."},
{q:"What was Naaman told to do?", options:["Go and wash in Jordan seven times","Wash once in Abana","Offer a sacrifice","Fast seven days"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:10",verse:"And Elisha sent a messenger unto him, saying, Go and wash in the Jordan seven times, and thy flesh shall come again to thee, and thou shalt be clean.", insight:"Simple, humbling, repeated; obedience, not grandeur, is the channel of grace."},
{q:"What had Naaman expected Elisha to do?", options:["Come out, stand, call on the name of the LORD his God, and strike his hand over the place","Anoint him with oil","Take his gold","Pray all night"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:11",verse:"But Naaman was wroth, and went away, and said, Behold, I thought, He will surely come out to me, and stand, and call on the name of the LORD his God, and strike his hand over the place, and recover the leper.", insight:"He had scripted his own miracle; pride writes the program, then resents the Director."},
{q:"Which rivers did Naaman name as better than all the waters of Israel?", options:["Abana and Pharpar, rivers of Damascus","Euphrates and Tigris","Nile and Jordan","Kishon and Jabbok"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:12",verse:"Are not Abana and Pharpar, rivers of Damascus, better than all the waters of Israel? may I not wash in them, and be clean? So he turned and went away in a rage.", insight:"He compared rivers and missed the point; the power was never in the water but in the word."},
{q:"How did Naaman's servants persuade him?", options:["If the prophet had bid thee do some great thing, wouldest thou not have done it? how much rather, Wash, and be clean?","The king commands thee","Thy honour requires it","The rivers are cursed"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:13",verse:"And his servants came near, and spake unto him, and said, My father, if the prophet had bid thee do some great thing, wouldest thou not have done it? how much rather then, when he saith to thee, Wash, and be clean?", insight:"Servants reasoned where pride raged; wise counsel often comes from below, not above."},
{q:"What happened when Naaman dipped seven times in Jordan?", options:["His flesh came again like unto the flesh of a little child, and he was clean","Nothing changed at first","The water turned bitter","He grew angry again"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:14",verse:"Then went he down, and dipped himself seven times in Jordan, according to the saying of the man of God: and his flesh came again like unto the flesh of a little child, and he was clean.", insight:"Childlike flesh for a humbled captain; God restores what pride had withered."},
{q:"What did Naaman confess after his healing?", options:["Now I know that there is no God in all the earth, but in Israel","Elisha is the greatest prophet","The Jordan is holy","I will conquer Israel"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:15",verse:"And he returned to the man of God, he and all his company, and came, and stood before him: and he said, Behold, now I know that there is no God in all earth, but in Israel: now therefore, I pray thee, take a blessing of thy servant.", insight:"A Syrian general preached the first sermon of the chapter; healing that does not end in confession is unfinished."},
{q:"What did Elisha answer when Naaman urged a gift upon him?", options:["As the LORD liveth, before whom I stand, I will receive none","Take thy gifts to the poor","Give half to the king","Keep them for thy journey"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:16",verse:"But he said, As the LORD liveth, before whom I stand, I will receive none. And he urged him to take it; but he refused.", insight:"He refused payment for grace; free healing must stay free, or it ceases to preach."},
{q:"What unusual request did Naaman make before departing?", options:["Two mules' burden of earth, to worship the LORD upon it","A house in Samaria","Elisha's mantle","A letter to the king"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:17",verse:"And Naaman said, Shall there not then, I pray thee, be given to thy servant two mules’ burden of earth? for thy servant will henceforth offer neither burnt offering nor sacrifice unto other gods, but unto the LORD.", insight:"He wanted Israel's soil under his altar; new faith looks for ground to stand on."},
{q:"For what did Naaman ask the LORD's pardon in advance?", options:["That when he must bow in the house of Rimmon with his master, the LORD would pardon him","For his past idolatry","For his anger at Elisha","For taking the earth"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:18",verse:"In this thing the LORD pardon thy servant, that when my master goeth into the house of Rimmon to worship there, and he leaneth on my hand, and I bow myself in the house of Rimmon: when I bow down myself in the house of Rimmon, the LORD pardon thy servant in this thing.", insight:"A new convert's tender conscience; grace meets us even in the duties we cannot yet escape."},
{q:"What did Gehazi resolve when he saw his master refuse the gifts?", options:["I will run after Naaman, and take somewhat of him","I will rebuke my master","I will follow Naaman to Syria","I will tell the king"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:20",verse:"But Gehazi, the servant of Elisha the man of God, said, Behold, my master hath spared Naaman this Syrian, in not receiving at his hands that which he brought: but, as the LORD liveth, I will run after him, and take somewhat of him.", insight:"The servant's heart priced what the prophet's refused; greed begins the moment grace is refused."},
{q:"What did Gehazi answer when Elisha asked where he had been?", options:["Thy servant went no whither","I went to pray","I followed thy command","I was in the city"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:25",verse:"But he went in, and stood before his master. And Elisha said unto him, Whence comest thou, Gehazi? And he said, Thy servant went no whither.", insight:"One lie to cover greed; hidden sin always needs a second sin to hide it."},
{q:"What judgment fell upon Gehazi?", options:["The leprosy of Naaman shall cleave unto thee, and unto thy seed for ever; and he went out a leper as white as snow","He was cast out of Israel","He lost his place as servant","He was struck blind"], a:0, ref:"2 Kings 5:27",verse:"The leprosy therefore of Naaman shall cleave unto thee, and unto thy seed for ever. And he went out from his presence a leper as white as snow.", insight:"He chased Naaman's silver and caught Naaman's leprosy; what we grasp in greed, we wear in judgment."}
]}
]);
